      "target": "For every finite simple undirected graph G on a labeled vertex set V with n=|V| divisible by 3, compute in polynomial time a graph H on the same vertex set satisfying Δ((V, E(G) symmetric-difference E(H))) <= 1 and either (a) a partition of V into n/3 triples, each inducing a triangle in H, or (b) nil with a correct guarantee that H has no triangle partition. Equivalently, prove that Sidestep(Triangle Partition, dist_Δ, 1) is in FP; or rigorously disprove that exact membership claim.",
      "title": "Triangle Partition Sidestep at maximum-degree edit radius one"
